course: dictionary
lesson: 16129
title: Whiskers, and other meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Whiskers is one of these words. It usually means the long, stiff hairs near an animal's mouth. «The cat's whiskers twitched as it sniffed the gap in the fence.» Here the cat is using its whiskers to feel the air, so the word means animal hairs.
explain: Whiskers can also mean the hair that grows on a man's face. «Dad shaved his whiskers before the wedding.» You can tell this from the word shaved, because you shave a face, not a cat.
explain: Watch out for the phrase «by a whisker». It has nothing to do with hair. «We won the race by a whisker.» The words around it tell you it means by a tiny amount, so the winners were only just ahead.
fact: Whiskers are long, stiff hairs that grow near the mouth and nose of animals such as cats, dogs, mice and seals.
fact: Whiskers are used for feeling things around the animal, especially in the dark.
fact: Whisker is the singular, so one hair is a whisker and many hairs are whiskers.
fact: «By a whisker» means by a tiny amount, as in «We won by a whisker».
fact: Seals use their whiskers to find fish in murky water, where they cannot see well.
exercise: «The cat's whiskers twitched as it felt the air near the gap.» What are whiskers? | Teeth used for tearing food | Claws used for climbing trees | *Long, stiff hairs near the mouth and nose, used for feeling things | Ears that hear very quietly
exercise: «We won the race by a whisker.» What does «by a whisker» mean? | *By a tiny amount | By a very large amount | Without any help at all | Running very fast with hair on your face
exercise: Which animal uses its whiskers to find fish in murky water? | Hen | Frog | Bee | *Seal
test: «The mouse's whiskers brushed the dark wall as it crept along.» Why does the mouse use its whiskers? | *To feel its way in the dark | To make a loud noise like a horn | To carry its food home | To sing a song
test: «Grandad stroked his whiskers as he thought hard about the puzzle.» What does stroking whiskers show? | He is angry and shouting | He is asleep in his chair | He is feeling cold | *He is thinking
exam: Which sentence uses whiskers to mean the hair on a man's face? | «The cat's whiskers twitched at the sound.» | *«Dad shaved his whiskers before the wedding.» | «The seal's whiskers helped it find fish.» | «We won the race by a whisker.»
